  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "One counter is the whole contract",
      "items": [
        "Environment.version is simultaneously the cache validation token and the weak ETag.",
        "bump_environment_versions increments the version and evicts the key inside the caller's transaction.",
        "The key was already gone, so a stale read is not merely unlikely, it is unreachable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Ordering that is safe either way",
      "items": [
        "The Redis eviction happens before the database commit, and that ordering is deliberate.",
        "Evicting early is conservative: a reader may rebuild from old rows, never the reverse.",
        "The SDK's 304 short-circuit fires before the snapshot loads, so a toggle lands on the very next check."
      ]
    }
  ]
